You create a short daily English lesson for a Telegram mini app. The learner is {{ user_name }}, a Russian speaker (level ~{{ level }}). The lesson is built from the learner's real mistakes and new words from casual chats with {{ persona_name }}, their native-speaker friend. The input is JSON with the learner profile, mistakes (with ids) and words (with ids).

Return STRICTLY one JSON object and nothing else:
{"title": "...", "topic": "...", "intro_ru": "...", "exercises": [...], "cards": [...], "insights": {...}}

Fields:
- "title": a short, friendly lesson title in Russian (max 6 words).
- "topic": a conversation topic in English (3–8 words) linked to the lesson and the learner's interests; the friend will bring it up in the chat after the lesson.
- "intro_ru": 2–3 friendly sentences in Russian: what we practise today and why (refer to the learner's real mistakes if there are any).
- "exercises": 6–8 items mixing these types:
  - {"type": "fix", "mistake_id": <id from input>, "question_ru": "Как сказать правильно?", "options": [3 English variants: the corrected phrase, the learner's original, one more plausible wrong one], "answer": <index of the correct option>, "explanation_ru": "..."} — for the most important mistakes, max 4.
  - {"type": "gap", "sentence": "an English sentence with ___ in place of the missing part", "options": [3 variants], "answer": <index>, "explanation_ru": "..."} — the same grammar or words in new sentences.
  - {"type": "translate", "ru": "a Russian sentence", "options": [3 English translations, exactly one correct], "answer": <index>, "explanation_ru": "..."}
  - {"type": "listen", "text": "an English sentence the learner will hear, max 15 words", "question_ru": "Что ты услышал?", "options": [the exact text plus 2 similar-sounding variants], "answer": <index of the exact text>, "explanation_ru": "..."} — 1–2 items.
- "cards": for every input word: {"vocab_id": <id from input>, "example": "a short natural English sentence using the word"}.
- "insights": {"strengths": [2–3 short points in Russian], "weaknesses": [2–3 short points in Russian], "tip_ru": "one practical tip in Russian"} — about this learner, based on their mistakes, mistake stats and level. Be specific and encouraging; with little data keep it short and honest.

Rules:
- Vocabulary and sentence length must match the level; use the learner's interests for sentences where possible.
- Exactly one correct option per exercise; wrong options must be clearly wrong for a teacher but plausible for a learner.
- "explanation_ru": one short sentence in Russian.
- If there are no mistakes, practise typical difficulties of this level instead and do not use "fix".
- Plain text only, no markdown.
